Let Let x is the change in concentration.

|   | Fe<sup>3+</sup>  (mol/L) | KCN (mol/L) | Fe(CN)<sub>6</sub><sup>4</sup> (mol/L) |
|---|---|---|---|
| Initial | 1.0 | 0.50 | 0 |
| Change | -x | -6x | +x |
| Equilibrium | 1.0 - x | 0.50 - 6x | x |

**3.  Write the K<sub>eq</sub> Expression**

K<sub>eq</sub> = [Fe(CN)<sub>6</sub><sup>4</sup>] / [Fe<sup>3+</sup>]

**4.  Substitute ICE Table Values into K<sub>Eq</sub> Equation**

1.2 x 10<sup>20</sup> = [x] / [1.0 - x]

