$$F(x, y, y) = x^2 + y^2 + 9y^2 = 56$$
We find the directional vector of the tangent vector to the surface at the point $(4, 2, -2)$.
We compute the directional vector by taking the partial part parts of $F(x, y, y)$ with the partial partial parts of $x, y, z$:
$$ \frac{\partial F}{\partial x} = 2x, \quad \frac{\partial F}{\partial y} = 2y, \quad \frac{\partial F}{\partial z} = 18y $$
At the point $(4, 2, -2)$, we have
$$ \frac{\partial F}{\partial x}(4, 2, -2) = 2(4) = 8 \\ \frac{\partial F}{\partial y}(4, 2, - -2) = 2(2) = 4 \\ \frac{\partial F}{\partial z}(4, 2, -2) = 18(-2) = -36 $$
