The circumference of the circle is $2\pi s = 2\pi (1) = 2\pi$.
The fraction of the circle is $\frac{\text{circum circumference of the base of the circle}}{\text{circum circumference of the circle}} = \frac{\frac{3}{4}\pi}{2\pi} = \frac{3}{4} \cdot \frac{1}{2} = \frac{3}{8}$.
The central angle is $\frac{3}{8} \times 360^\circ = \frac{3 \times 360}{8} = \3 \times 45 = 135^\circ$.

Final answer:
The correct answer is 135 degrees.

