$$ 2 \sum_{k=1}^{n} x^k = 2 \frac{x(1 - x^n)}{1 - x} \text{ for } x \neq \pm1. $$

Combine all parts to form the entire sum:
$$ S_n = \frac{x^2 - x^{2n+2}}{1 - x^2} + 2 \frac{x - x^{n+1}}{1 - x} + n. $$

