","The calculation of the electron-loss (EOS) or core-loss (CO) spectrum, which is directly related to the momentum-loss power and therefore the momentum-loss cross time time, for the emission of electron-loss ones-orbiton (plasiton) in the interaction of low-energy electrons with a 3d-electron-local-order (LO) electron-momentum-action (EO) theory is a complex, many-term integral.  However, a simplified, simplified-Hartier-Pron-Hartson (Harton) formula provides a good approximation for the integrated integral-time-time (IIO) of the electron-loss (EO) spectrum, and the reduced-loss-loss (RLO) of the electron-loss (EO) spectrum.

Here, I will break the breakdown of the calculation and present the simplified formula.  It assumes a 3d-electron-local-order (EO) model and a Druden-model for the electron-density-state (EO) density.

**Conceptual Framework:**

* **Electron-Loss (EO) Process:**  A low-energy electron interacts with the material, transferring energy and momentum.  If the energy transferred is equal to the momentum-length-dimension (EO) of a 2d-electron-like (LO) phonon (pll), the electron loses energy and a plasiton is created.
* **Density-Sum-Time (EO) Theory:** This is a quantum-time-time (TO) theory that describes the interaction of electrons with the electron-density-state (EO) of the system.
