\[
I = \frac{1}{2} m r^2 = \frac{1}{2} \times 1 \times (0.5)^2 = 0.125 \, \text{kg} \cdot \text{m}^2
\]
Substituting \( \tau = I \alpha \):
\[
F \cdot r = I \alpha
\]

### Step 4: Solve for the Force \( F \)
Substitute the known values:
\[
F \times 0.5 = 0.125 \times 4
\]
\[
F \times 0.5 = 0.5
\]
\[
F = \frac{0.5}{0.5} = 1 \, \text{N}
\]

